1
00:00:00,100 --> 00:00:02,783
Skills run on your machine with access to your files.

2
00:00:02,733 --> 00:00:06,025
That means you need to treat them like you'd treat any third-party dependency.

3
00:00:06,025 --> 00:00:11,950
The three risks that matter most: prompt injection — someone could hide instructions in a document that override your skill's behavior.

4
00:00:11,950 --> 00:00:16,641
Supply chain — installing a skill from an author you don't know is like running a random npm package.

5
00:00:16,641 --> 00:00:21,933
And data exfiltration — a malicious script could read your environment variables or config files and send them somewhere.

6
00:00:21,933 --> 00:00:23,866
The defenses are straightforward.

7
00:00:23,866 --> 00:00:26,191
Read the SKILL.md before installing.

8
00:00:26,191 --> 00:00:27,858
Check the scripts folder.

9
00:00:27,858 --> 00:00:29,991
Only install from authors you trust.

10
00:00:29,991 --> 00:00:33,150
If a skill does something that surprises you, don't install it.

11
00:00:33,150 --> 00:00:34,191
Period.

